  "answer": "### Issue Presented\n\nHowever, if there are reasonable grounds to believe that their gross sales will exceed ₱3 million in the next 12 months, they may still need to register. It is advisable for the designer to monitor their income closely and consider voluntary registration if they anticipate growth.\n\n**Legal Basis:**\n- **NIRC Sec. 236**: Outlines the registration requirements for VAT.\n\nIn summary, the graphic designer is not required to register for VAT based on their current gross receipts, but they should remain vigilant about their income projections.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
